From 0659d3404bbc3976762bd60dc9b1f3d59d7a1e35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas <yusenrong46@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:18:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Keep Luna retries within one budget under Vercel's 120s
 limit

Each provider attempt used the full chat timeout regardless of time already spent,
so the default worst case was about 110s and allowed settings reached about 375s.
Attempts now share a 100s per-turn budget (later attempts get only what remains,
and a retry starts only if it can still fit), connect/write phases are capped, and a
chat timeout that cannot fit is reported by readiness. The browser waits 125s for
chat and follow-up calls instead of retrying at 60s while the first call could
still reach Luna.

Tests: three budget cases in test_openrouter_conversation_contract.py (all fail on
the previous loop: 110.15s worst case, extra retries) and the config readiness case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
